QuestGuidance.Register("en",420,{
[13409]="7000D1A9\n1\tTalk to Bill Twiggins\tBill Twiggins is in the market square of the Bree homestead. Nan Henwood has sent you to speak with Bill Twiggins in hopes that he can help you furnish your home.\n",
[13410]="70009EC2\n1\tSlaughter the Free People in Tírith Rhaw (total: 6)\tSlaughter the Free Peoples within the bounds of Tírith Rhaw. Fandmau seems unimpressed with your capability, but you can show him that you are more of a soldier of Angmar than he.\n2\tTalk to Soldier Fandmau\030Talk to War-tyrant Akúlhun\tIf Fandmau was killed or Tírith Rhaw was lost, make your way to War-tyrant Akúlhun at Gramsfoot. Fandmau's fears were unfounded. You repelled the attack and scored a great victory over the Free People. You should return to him with your report.\n",
[13411]="70048C92\n1\tDefeat gory Huorns (total: 5)\tGory Huorns can be found in the wilds of Agarnaith, near Seregost. You should defeat gory Huorns.\n2\tCompleted.\t\n",
[13412]="700654B4\n1\tExamine the first site\030Examine the second site\030Examine the third site\030Examine the fourth site\030Examine the fifth site\030Examine the sixth site\tBirási has asked you to inspect the braces supporting walls and other stonework at various sites in the Harlond.\n2\tReturn to Birási\tYou have examined Birási's assigned inspection sites. You should let him know what you found. Birási is in the Harlond.\n",
[13413]="70035011\n1\tFree the farmers (0/4)\tThe farmers survived their capture at Thrymm's Farm. They appear to be relatively healthy, all things considered. After all they have been through, they should at least have their freedom.\n2\tThe farmers survived their capture at Thrymm's Farm. They appear to be relatively healthy, all things considered. After all they have been through, they should at least have their freedom.\t\n3\tAfter being freed, the farmers have likely made their way back to the safety of Forlaw. You should head to the tavern since after surviving such an ordeal, some ale would look promising to anyone.\t\n4\tSpeak with Gárwig in Lornsettle\tGárwig is in Lornsettle, the mead hall of Forlaw. He will be happy to know the farmers have safely returned.\n",
[13414]="700160E0\n1\tTalk to Gufi to travel to the mine-site\tGufi is at the Menem-berej encampment in the centre of the Silvertine Lodes. You should speak with Gufi to travel to the prospective mining site.\n2\tTalk to Gufi at Menem-berej\tGufi is at the Menem-berej encampment in the centre of the Silvertine Lodes. You should speak with Gufi about the survey-expedition.\n",
[13415]="700097E2\n1\tDefeat Jabe Grimshaw\tJabe Grimshaw plans his band's attacks from atop Barad Rath, a flat stone overlook atop the tall hills of Tyrn Fornech, north-east of Tinnudir and north of Tham Ornen. Ranger Naethmunn has asked you to find and defeat Jabe Grimshaw, leader of a band of tomb-robbers that has plagued the Rangers of Evendim for a long time.\n2\tTalk to Naethmunn\tNaethmunn is at the Ranger-camp on the island of Tinnudir, in Evendim, south-west of Barad Rath. You should report your victory over Jabe Grimshaw to Naethmunn.\n",
[13416]="7006C0B3\n1\tTBD collect crocodile hides (total: 10)\tTBD collect crocodile hide\n2\tTBD return to the curious tanner with the hides\tTBD give the croc hides to the curious tanner\n",
[13417]="70009E0E\n1\tTalk to Leighton Kipps and aid the Rangers\tLeighton Kipps is at the spies' camp in the south-east of Rantost. Leighton Kipps is waiting to signal the Rangers to assault Rantost.\n2\tTalk to Eliot Bencroft on Rantost\tEliot Bencroft is at the south-east of Rantost. Eliot Bencroft will be pleased to hear the Rangers were able to recover their relics and the spies can return to Ost Forod.\n",
[13418]="70009E12\n1\tRecover the stolen treasure\tThe robber-camp is on a tiny island at the mouth of the Brandywine river in Lake Evendim. Having successfully defeated the brigands at Rantost Island, you have been sent to another small brigand camp, where it is hoped you will be able to recover some more stolen treasure.\n2\tDefeat Ned Leggett\tYou have discovered a tomb-robber ambush.\n3\tTalk to Balchelos\tBalchelos is back at Tinnudir. You overcame the tomb-robber ambush and should report the incident to Balchelos.\n",
[13419]="7001BF38\n1\tClaim the South-gate\tThe first step to driving the brigands out of Bree is to reclaim the South-gate and gain access to the city itself.\n2\tClaim the Auction Hall\tWith the South-gate claimed, you can move on to the southern courtyard and the Auction House, a crucial hub of commerce.\n3\tClaim the haunted alley\tThe way north has been blocked and barricaded by giant snow mounds, you will have to head west through the haunted alley.\n4\tClaim the Jailhouse\tClaiming the Jailhouse will provide a convenient place to lockup those that remain once the city is back under the control of the Free Peoples.\n5\tClaim the courtyard\tWithout control of the courtyard, you cannot hope to assault and claim Town Hall.\n6\tClaim the Town Hall\tAll that remains is to claim Town Hall and see the banner of Bree-town fly high over it.\n",
[13420]="70029FC5\n1\tComplete 'Thievery and Mischief' in a raid group\tWhile the Rangers of the North were distracted in the South, brigands and ruffians took an opportunity to wrest control of Bree....\n",
[13421]="7004CE3C\n1\tDestroy river nets (total: 10)\tRiver nets can be found along the Forest River between Loeglond and Felegoth. You should destroy river nets.\n2\tTalk to Lorndúr\tLorndúr can be found in Loeglond. You should talk to Lorndúr.\n",
[13422]="70066748\n1\tCollect stolen goods in Tarlang's Crown (0/12)\tStolen goods can be found in Azruthor's Rue and throughout Tarlang's Crown. While exploring the ruined remains of Azruthor's encampment in Tarlang's Crown, you have found a number of stolen goods. You should collect the stolen goods.\n2\tCollect stolen goods in Tarlang's Crown (total: 12)\tStolen goods can be found in Azruthor's Rue and throughout Tarlang's Crown. While exploring the ruined remains of Azruthor's encampment in Tarlang's Crown, you have found a number of stolen goods. You should collect the stolen goods.\n3\tDeliver the stolen goods to Amathon in Sardol\tAmathon can be found in Sardol in the Blackroot Vale. You have collected a number of stolen goods from the Corsairs and Gondorian traitors at Azruthor's Rue. You should deliver them to Amathon.\n",
[13423]="70072BFA\n1\tExamine the cocooned body\tThe spiders of Narchásh snare their victims in cocoons.\n2\tDefeat spiders at Narchásh (total: 6)\030Examine another cocooned body at Narchásh\tYou have decided to combat the spiders of Narchásh and search for any survivors of their deadly hunger.\n3\tLeave the Kinta bracelet in a strongbox at Laivárth, the Kinta grove to the north-east\tThe nearest grove of the Kintai should be Laivárth, located to the north-east of Narchásh. The Elves there will have a strongbox in which you can deposit the Kinta bracelet.\n4\tCompleted\tYou have left the Kinta bracelet in the strongbox at Laivárth, where it can be retrieved by one of the people to whom it should be entrusted.\n",
[13424]="7006749B\n1\tReturn the necklace to Nûrat\030Recover the sentimental necklace from Gunjik in the camp of Grijâti\tNûrat asked you to make your way south along the road outside of Jax Phanâl and then turn west toward Grijâti, the camp of Haradrim there. Among the Haradrim is a warrior named Gunjik, who stole something precious from her. She wants it back.\n",
[13425]="7005B185\n1\tCollect trophy-beards from the Ufúrzrak at Muru Azog\tTrophy-beards are carried by the Ufúrzrak at Muru Azog, before the East-gate of Nud-mekhem at Azanulbizar. You should collect trophy-beards from the Ufúrzrak.\n2\tCollect trophy-beards from the Ufúrzrak at Muru Azog (total: 12)\tTrophy-beards are carried by the Ufúrzrak at Muru Azog, before the East-gate of Nud-mekhem at Azanulbizar. You should collect trophy-beards from the Ufúrzrak.\n3\tCompleted\tYou have collected many trophy-beards from the Orcs of the Ufúrzrak at Muru Azog.\n",
[13426]="70028AD2\n1\tDefeat Dragon-clan thieves at the Galtrev Lumber-camp (total: 10)\tDragon-clan brigands and thieves roam the Galtrev Lumber-camp. You should defeat a number of Dunlending thieves to secure the Galtrev Lumber-camp.\n2\tTalk to Fraid at his waggon\tFraid awaits you near his broken waggon in Pren Gwydh, not far from the Galtrev Lumber-camp. You should speak with Fraid and let him know that the woods are a little safer now.\n",
[13427]="7006D1C8\n1\tDefeat Corsairs (total: 12)\030Collect Númenórean artifacts (total: 8)\tDefeat the thieving Corsairs to stop them from digging up more artifacts, and collect the relics they have already uncovered to return them to the Ambarûli.\n",
[13428]="70043225\n1\tRecover stolen goods from Haradrim archers (total: 8)\tHaradrim archers can be found to the east and north-east of Halach in Upper Lebennin. Gorhir has asked you to recover goods stolen by Haradrim archers in their last raid against Halach.\n2\tDeliver the recovered goods to Gorhir in Halach\tGorhir can be found in Halach in south-eastern Upper Lebennin. You have recovered many of the stolen goods and should now return them to Gorhir in Halach.\n",
[13429]="7000887C\n1\tReturn to Lieutenant Solvi at Tol Ascarnen\030Collect food-sacks (total: 10)\tFood-sacks might be found on the Orcs, trolls, and goblins in the Ettenmoors. Lieutenant Solvi advised you to search Grothum and Dâr-gazag for more plentiful amounts of the food-sacks, but also said that the Ongbúrz and Snowreap may have some on their persons.\n",
[13430]="70040384\n1\tRecover stolen coin-purses from corsair toughs\tThe Corsairs from Umbar have set up camp in the swamp in north-eastern Lamedon. You should recover stolen coin-purses from the Corsairs in Tathrendalf, their large and swampy encampment.\n2\tSearch Corsairs for stolen coin-purses (total: 10)\tThe Corsairs from Umbar have set up camp in the swamp in north-eastern Lamedon. You should recover stolen coin-purses from the Corsairs in Tathrendalf, their large and swampy encampment.\n3\tCompleted\tYou have recovered a number of stolen coin-purses from the Corsairs who have set up their camp in the swamps of northern Lamedon.\n",
[13431]="7004E980\n1\tDefeat Karazgar, the Weeping Warrior\030Defeat Athramóth\030Defeat Frór the Lost\030Defeat Karkasht Crow-feeder\tDefeat the inhabitants of Thikil-gundu, the Steel Keep.\n",
[13432]="7004E989\n1\tDefeat Karazgar, the Weeping Warrior\030Defeat Athramóth\030Defeat Frór the Lost\030Defeat Karkasht Crow-feeder\tDefeat the inhabitants of Thikil-gundu, the Steel Keep.\n",
[13433]="7004E98A\n1\tDefeat Karazgar, the Weeping Warrior\030Defeat Athramóth\030Defeat Frór the Lost\030Defeat Karkasht Crow-feeder\tDefeat the inhabitants of Thikil-gundu, the Steel Keep.\n",
[13434]="70050213\n1\tDefeat invaders within Thikil-gundu (total: 25)\tDefeat invaders within Thikil-gundu\n2\tCompleted\tDefeat invaders within Thikil-gundu\n",
[13435]="700501E5\n1\tDefeat Zánmog\tDefeat Zánmog within Thikil-gundu.\n2\tTalk to Stráhek the Stout\tYou should return to to Stráhek the Stout in Skarháld and let him know of your success.\n",
[13436]="70050214\n1\tGather tomes of knowledge (total: 10)\tGather tomes of knowledge.\n2\tCompleted\tGather tomes of knowledge.\n",
[13437]="7001E995\n1\tDefeat Wargs (total: 15)\tThe Wargs make their den in Naur-hoit, south of Mithechad. Perindúr has asked you to hunt down and defeat the Wargs of the Ashenslades.\n2\tTalk to Perindúr at Mithechad\tPerindúr is at Mithechad, north of Naur-hoit. You should return to Perindúr with news of your success against the Wargs of the Ashenslades.\n",
[13438]="70054664\n1\tDefeat Gothmog's defenders (total: 8)\030Defeat Gothmog's scouts (total: 8)\tGothmog's scouts and defenders are patrolling the area and must be defeated. You should defeat Orc scouts and defenders.\n2\tTalk to Dolenthol\tYou thinned the ranks of Gothmog's forces in the area. You should return to Dolenthol and inform him of your success.\n",
[13439]="70015E1B\n1\tTalk to Golgallon at Echad Eregion\tGolgallon is at Echad Eregion, far to the south-east of Gwingris. Maedlathron has asked you to warn Golgallon that the Company may have left further signs of their passing in the wild.\n",
[13440]="700494BC\n1\tEnter Thorzhaf\tThorzhaf can be found in Talath Úrui. You should enter Thorzhaf.\n2\tSteal an Orc blade to look more like a fighter\tThorzhaf can be found in Talath Úrui. You should find a suitable Orc blade to steal in Thorzhaf.\n3\tTalk to Maukatish\tMaukatish can be found at Thorzhaf. You should speak with Maukatish about signing up to participate in the pit-fighting tournament.\n",
